# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Communication Protocol

This project uses loom's [Seam Artifact Protocol](https://github.com/zentetsukenz/agent) so
context survives when ownership changes hands between agents/sessions. It is the shared contract
every agent and skill that hands off context references — read it before producing or discovering
a handoff.

> This document is generated by loom's OpenCode setup ([ADR-011](../../wiki/adr/adr-011-seam-artifact-protocol.md)).
> It is committed to the repo (OpenCode has no memory tool and no `handoffs:` primitive, so the
> ledger *is* these files). Change the choices below by re-running the guided `update`.

## Ledger

- **Substrate:** committed folder (repo-visible, survives sessions).
- **Ledger root:** `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}`   <!-- default .loom/handoffs/ -->
- **Namespace:** `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}<stage>/<milestone-slug>/*.md` (human-readable slug, not a timestamp)
- **Manifest:** `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}index.md` — one row per seam artifact; **latest row for a milestone wins**.
- **Wired into context:** this file's path is listed in `opencode.json`'s `instructions:` array, so
  every agent loads it.

## Seam artifacts per stage

| Stage seam | Producer (writes at exit gate) | Artifacts | Consumer (discovers at entry gate) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Shaping → Delivery** | Shaping agent | {{SHAPING_ARTIFACTS}} | Planner |
| **Delivery → Closing** | Orchestrator (via Verifier evidence) | {{DELIVERY_ARTIFACTS}} | Closing agent |
| **Closing (final)** | Closing agent | {{CLOSING_ARTIFACTS}} | — (closes the trail) |

Producing the seam artifact is **mandatory at these two stage seams** — a stage's exit gate is not
satisfied until the artifact is written and its manifest row registered. Within a stage
(phase-to-phase, dispatcher → utility) handoff is advisory.

## The transition (no automatic handoff)

OpenCode has no `handoffs:` primitive. The transition between stages is:

1. The producing **primary agent** writes the artifacts + manifest row at its exit gate.
2. The human **`Tab`-selects the next stage's primary agent** (Shaping → Planner, Orchestrator →
   Closing).
3. That agent **DISCOVERs** the ledger at its entry gate before doing anything else.

## How to PRODUCE (at a stage exit)

1. Compress the session (invoke the `handoff` skill).
2. Write the stage's expected artifacts to `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}<stage>/<milestone-slug>/`.
   **Reference** PRDs/ADRs/commits/issues by path — never re-embed them.
3. Register a row in the manifest `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}index.md`:
   `| <milestone> | <stage> | <artifact-path> | <status> | <date> |`
   (status: `ready-for-delivery`, `shipped`, `preserved`, or `in-progress`).

## How to DISCOVER (at a stage entry)

1. Read the manifest `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}index.md`.
2. Find the latest `ready-for-*` / `shipped` row for the milestone you were asked to pick up.
3. Load **only** that artifact directory — keep the session-start context budget small.

## Manifest format

```markdown
# Handoff Ledger

| Milestone | Stage | Artifact | Status | Updated |
|---|---|---|---|---|
```
